# Vydon Frontend Rules

## Data fetching

- Always import `useQuery` and `useMutation` from `@connectrpc/connect-query`, not `@tanstack/react-query`.
  - The connect wrapper aligns with our API's generated types.
  - It uses TanStack Query under the hood — no need to import it directly.
- Do not synchronise server data with `useEffect`. Use `connect-query` queries instead.

## Components

- Function components only. No class components.
- Server Components by default. Add `'use client'` only when required (state, effects, browser APIs).
- Default export is reserved for Next.js pages and layouts. Reusable components use named exports.
- Prop types live in an `interface Props { ... }` above the component for any component with more than two props.

## File naming

- Components: `PascalCase.tsx` (e.g. `BaseLayout.tsx`, `SiteHeader.tsx`).
- Providers / hooks / utilities: `kebab-case.ts` (e.g. `query-provider.tsx`, `use-account.ts`).
- Next.js routing files keep their framework convention (`page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`).

## Imports

- Use the `@/*` path alias instead of relative parents (`../../`).
- Order: external packages, then `@/...`, then `./` relative imports.

## State

- Server state → `@connectrpc/connect-query`.
- Local UI state → `useState` / `useReducer`.
- Global state → typed React contexts. Do not introduce Redux or Zustand without justification.
- URL state → Next.js `searchParams`.
- Forms → `react-hook-form` + `zod`.

## TypeScript

- `strict: true` is mandatory. No `// @ts-ignore` — use `// @ts-expect-error` with a one-line reason if absolutely required.
- Generated proto types in `gen/` are read-only.
- `any` requires an inline comment explaining why.

## Linting / formatting

- Prettier: 2 spaces, single quotes, semicolons, `trailingComma: es5`. No per-file overrides.
- ESLint `no-console: error` (except `warn` and `error`).
- Unused vars must be prefixed `_` to be ignored.
- `knip --production --strict` must pass — remove unused exports.

## Performance

- `next/image` only, with explicit `width` and `height`. `priority` reserved for hero media.
- Use `dynamic(() => import(...))` for heavy non-critical components.

## Naming reminders

- Booleans: `is`, `has`, `should`, `can` prefixes.
- Hooks: `use` prefix.
- Constants: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE only for module-level magic numbers; otherwise camelCase.
